    "result_text": "All tests pass (4 total: 3 AddressResolver + 1 AcceptanceTest). Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), keeping each piece of logic in a small, single-responsibility unit and reusing it everywhere.\n\n**New unit \u2014 `util/FiscalYearResolver`**\nA dedicated resolver (mirroring the existing `*Resolver` utilities) that owns all fiscal-year logic:\n- `yearOf(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year, identified by the calendar year it ends in (a date on/after 1 July belongs to next year's FY).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 the `FY<YY>` string (null-safe).\n- `elapsedYears(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed, as a difference of fiscal years.\n\n**Wired in \u2014 reusing that one unit rather than duplicating date math:**\n- `MembershipNumberFormatter` \u2014 the `M<YY>` year segment now uses the fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date (e.g. a Sept 2026 date \u2192 `-M27`).\n- `MembershipLevelCalculator` \u2014 tenure now counts *elapsed fiscal years* (threshold constant renamed `TENURE_THRESHOLD_FISCAL_YEARS = 1`) instead of a 365-day window; dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 new `fiscalYear` mapping delegating to `FiscalYearResolver.label(...)`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it, and updated the `membershipNumber` description to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nBoth `fiscalYear` and `membershipNumber` derive from the stored registration date, which the controller has already adjusted to a business day before saving, so both are consistently business-day-adjusted.\n\nThe acceptance test (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) and all existing tests pass; the audit log confirms `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` for a 2026-09-16 registration.\n\nOne deliberate call worth flagging: I identified the fiscal year by its **ending** calendar year (so July 2026 \u2192 FY27) and set the tenure threshold to \"exceeds 1 elapsed fiscal year.\" The spec fixed the format and the 1-July start but not these two conventions, and no test pins them \u2014 say the word if you'd prefer the start-year label (FY26) or a different tenure boundary.",
